  "setup_observations": [
    "APT stale metadata returned 404 before installation. Metadata refresh was successful; the resulting libc upgrade proposal was not executed. Compiler payloads were extracted in the owned tool root instead.",
    "Full Linux header extraction met a case-insensitive filename collision on the Windows mounted filesystem. Revised extraction selected executable/library payloads only; partial headers remain because deletion was automatically denied.",
    "Component archive manifest.in names collided; revised extraction omitted component installer metadata and verified existing payload bytes before proceeding.",
    "Missing cached Cargo dependencies prevented the initial offline build; cargo fetch --locked --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu populated the existing developer cache. Cargo.lock stayed byte-identical.",
    "The compiler preflight first lacked cc, then linker-script runtime libraries. The successful isolated linker used hash-bound host runtime dependencies.",
    "An explicit Rust target left host build-script linker settings separate. A generated cc launcher initially contained literal backslash-n sequences; correcting its newline bytes allowed the same canonical build and tests to pass.",
    "Windows lstat could not inspect a dangling Linux tool link. Linux lstat inspected links without following them; cleanup selected only disjoint tool paths and never attempted the policy-blocked headers or a parent directory.",
    "WSL emitted a pre-existing unrelated Windows PATH translation warning; no global PATH or profile was changed.",
    "Shared C# compilation retained analyzer DLLs despite MSBuild node reuse being disabled. Graceful compiler-server shutdown released them; future bounded runs should also disable shared compilation."
  ],
